WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:02.270
- [Instructor] What I would
like to do in this video

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:05.070
is to see if we can prove

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.730
that triangle DCA

00:00:09.919 --> 00:00:13.107
is congruent to triangle BAC.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:16.560
Pause this video

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.910
and see if you can figure
that out on your own.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.910
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.070
So let's see what we can figure out.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:29.460
We see that segment DC is
parallel to segment AB,

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.420
that's what these little arrows tell us,

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.240
and so you can view this segment AC

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.570
as something of a transversal
across those parallel lines,

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.500
and we know that alternate interior angles

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.010
would be congruent, so we know for example

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.270
that the measure of this angle

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.620
is the same as the measure of this angle,

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.690
or that those angles are congruent.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.120
We also know that both of these triangles,

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.120
both triangle DCA and triangle
BAC, they share this side,

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.680
which by reflexivity is going
to be congruent to itself,

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:03.513
so in both triangles,

00:01:03.513 --> 00:01:07.910
we have an angle and a
side that are congruent,

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:10.253
but can we figure out anything else?

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:12.820
Well you might be tempted

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.770
to make a similar argument thinking

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:17.910
that this is parallel to that
'cause it looks parallel,

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.040
but you can't make that
assumption just based

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:20.873
on how it looks.

00:01:20.873 --> 00:01:22.080
If you did know that,

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.330
then you would be able to
make some other assumptions

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.580
about some other angles here
and maybe prove congruency.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:30.450
But it turns out, given the
information that we have,

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:33.820
we can't just assume that
because something looks parallel,

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.600
that, or because something
looks congruent that they are,

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.610
and so based on just
the information given,

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:41.680
we actually can't prove congruency.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:44.470
Now let me ask you a
slightly different question.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:45.580
Let's say

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:49.210
that we did give you a
little bit more information.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:51.410
Let's say we told you that the measure

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:54.780
of this angle right
over here is 31 degrees,

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:58.110
and the measure of this angle
right over here is 31 degrees.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:02.070
Can you now prove that
triangle DCA is congruent

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:03.173
to triangle BAC?

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.340
So let's see what we can deduce now.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:12.040
Well we know that AC is in both triangles,

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.540
so it's going to be congruent to itself,

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:16.000
and let me write that down.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.610
We know that segment AC

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:23.320
is congruent to segment AC,

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:28.053
it sits in both triangles,
and this is by reflexivity,

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.180
which is a fancy way of
saying that something

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:33.750
is going to be congruent to itself.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:38.750
Now we also see that AB is
parallel to DC just like before,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.830
and AC can be viewed as
part of a transversal,

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:45.867
so we can deduce that angle CAB,

00:02:47.435 --> 00:02:49.910
lemme write this down, I should
be doing different color,

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:51.577
we can deduce that angle CAB,

00:02:53.832 --> 00:02:54.665
CAB,

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.293
is congruent to angle ACD,

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.730
angle ACD,

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:08.297
because they are alternate,
alternate interior, interior,

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:14.970
angles, where a transversal
intersects two parallel lines.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:17.453
So, just to be clear,

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:21.050
this angle, which is CAB,

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:25.290
is congruent to this angle, which is ACD.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:29.850
And so now, we have two angles and a side,

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:33.520
two angles and a side, that are congruent,

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.300
so we can now deduce by
angle-angle-side postulate

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.860
that the triangles are indeed congruent.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:45.860
So we now know that triangle
DCA is indeed congruent

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.720
to triangle BAC

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:54.730
because of angle-angle-side congruency,

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.020
which we've talked about
in previous videos,

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:57.853
and just to be clear,

00:03:57.853 --> 00:03:59.940
sometimes people like
the two-column proofs,

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.230
I can make this look a little bit more

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:06.230
like a two column-proof by
saying these are my statements,

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.400
statement, and this is my
rationale right over here.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:12.893
And we're done.

